<Bindings>
    <!-- Auto-loaded from the addon folder. Deliberately NOT listed in the TOC:
         doing so loads it twice and the second pass silently wins.

         Note for anyone editing the prose in these comments: a double hyphen is
         illegal inside an XML comment, and the parser rejects the WHOLE file on
         one. That is not a cosmetic failure. It means zero bindings register,
         and the only in-combat weapon swap path this addon has goes with them,
         silently, with nothing but a LUA_WARNING at load to say so.

         The weapon swap is a CLICK binding on a SecureActionButton rather than
         a script binding, and that is the entire point of it. Out of combat the
         cursor state machine handles every slot. In combat nothing scripted can
         move a weapon: PickupInventoryItem is restricted under combat lockdown
         and EquipItemByName degrades to a pickup. A secure button carrying
         macrotext, fired by a hardware keypress, is the only channel that
         works, so this binding is not a convenience. It is the sole in-combat
         path. -->
    <Binding name="CLICK CommanderArmoryEquipWeapons:LeftButton" header="COMMANDERARMORY" runOnUp="false"/>

    <Binding name="COMMANDERARMORY_TOGGLE" runOnUp="false">
        CommanderArmory_Toggle()
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
